    "etymology": {
     "text": "A corruption of medieval 是物 (‘what’) or 什物 (‘miscellaneous items’), perhaps influenced by 何物 (‘what’).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Taiwan usually writes 什麼 or 甚麼; both are traditional forms of 什么."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "No 吗 with a 什么 question: 你喝什么？ — with 吗, 什么 means ‘anything’: 你喝什么吗？ ‘Will you drink anything?’",
     "Word order does not change: put 什么 where the answer goes (你喝什么？— 我喝茶)."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "Before a noun, 什么 asks ‘what kind / which’: 什么菜？ ‘what dish?’.",
     "In fast speech it is often shéme."
    ]
